# Harness artifacts. Patterns here are relative to .claude/, and they cover the
# layer that *writes* the project — not the project itself, which the root
# .gitignore owns. Keeping the two apart means a rule about how the code gets
# written never has to be read as a rule about the code.
#
# The rest of this directory IS committed — agents, skills, hooks, commands,
# settings.json, MILESTONE. The harness enforces the invariants, and a
# contributor who clones without it loses every guard while the gate still says
# green. Only the machine-specific half stays out.

# Absolute home paths and personal permission grants. Correct on one machine,
# wrong on every other.
settings.local.json

# Hook state: markers and logs written between turns. Per checkout by design —
# a shared $TMPDIR name collides between two clones of this repo on one machine,
# and a stale marker there makes a hook stay silent when it should speak.
hooks/state/
